  m_Name: Scene13_Context
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.SceneAgentContext
  sceneId: Scene13
  sceneTitle: Ohm's Law
  askWattsonEnabled: 1
  covered:
  - "Everything from Scenes 5 to 12: voltage V (the push, volt), current I (the flow,
    ampere), resistance R (the opposition, ohm), V \u221D I for the nichrome wire
    at constant temperature, V/I constant, slope = R, 1 \u03A9 = 1 V / 1 A, this
    wire's R = 5 \u03A9."
  - 'Ohm''s law: V = IR. The potential difference across a conductor equals the current
    through it times its resistance, at constant temperature.'
  - 'If asked about the Christmas lights, give only a hint: think about which battery
    could keep a bigger potential difference across the lights.'
  doNotSpoil:
  - The full explanation of the Christmas-lights mystery (the Scene 14 video does
    that)
  faq: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0bde23866b05136459ee6622ad84af7c, type: 2}
